            Past performance is not indicative of future results. Historical data and back-testing do not guarantee future profitability.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Leverage Risk -->
      <section id="leverage" class="risk-card p-6 fade-in">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-amber-600/20 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-400">⚖️</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Leverage Risk</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Amplified gains and losses</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-800/20 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Amplified Losses</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm">
              While leverage can amplify profits, it also amplifies losses. A small market movement against your position can result in significant losses, potentially exceeding your initial deposit.
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-700">
                  <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-medium">Leverage</th>
